# Code Quality

Aim for production-grade clarity, safety, and maintainability on every change.

## Principles

- Prefer small, focused modules and functions with one clear job
- Clarity over cleverness; delete dead code; avoid speculative abstractions
- Fail loudly: no empty `catch`, no swallowed errors, no silent fallbacks that hide bugs
- Name things by intent; avoid abbreviations unless project-local and obvious
- Keep diffs tight — only change what the task needs

## JavaScript / Svelte

- ESM + named exports; public helpers get brief JSDoc when types or contracts are non-obvious
- Validate inputs at boundaries (API, forms); trust less at the edge
- Avoid magic numbers/strings — use named constants or CSS/design tokens
- Do not leave `console.log` debugging in committed code
- Ask before adding dependencies; prefer the platform and existing libs

## Security

- Never commit secrets, service-role keys, or real `.env` values
- Client code may use `VITE_*` public values only
- Treat user input as untrusted

## Before finishing

- Match existing patterns in nearby files
- Ensure the change is readable without prior chat context
- Prefer verifying with `npm run build` when the change touches app entry, config, or shared lib
